# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R2), the
# program its refusal's `guess` fixes write.
#
# `unsupported/fixedbugs-563-a-macro-two-headers-define-two-ways-is-refused`
# binds `fixedbugs-563-cap.h` and then `fixedbugs-563-limit.h`, which define
# `LIMIT` two ways, and is refused. Its note drafts this header of the
# program's own, `fixedbugs-563-cap_fixedbugs-563-limit.h`: the first header,
# `#undef LIMIT`, the second. Both groups name it, so it is included once, and
# the program means what its order said: `cap` caps at 10, read before the
# second header defines 100.
extern "fixedbugs-563-cap_fixedbugs-563-limit.h"
    function cap(v: i32) -> i32
    function half(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(half(x: 6))
    print(cap(v: 50))
